    "result_text": "The only executable test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two are support classes), and it passes. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required changing `customerCode` from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence, plus rebuilding everything derived from it.\n\n**One file changed, one function changed** (`OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice.assignCustomerCode`) \u2014 the lowest-impact option, since that aspect is the sole point where `customerCode` is generated and it lives in a tiny 2-method class (minimal `WMC_other`).\n\nThe change:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of `city` (padded with `X` if shorter, matching the existing `LAST3` logic).\n- `NNNN` = per-city sequence, computed as `1 + count of existing owners in that city` via `findAll().stream().filter(...)` \u2014 no new repository method needed, so no extra file touched.\n\n**`membershipNumber` needed no edit**: it's built in `OwnerMapper` by concatenating `customerCode + \"-M\" + <YY>`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `TOW-SUR-0001-M26`). Anything derived from `customerCode` inherits the new format for free.\n\nI also updated the class Javadoc to describe the new format (comment-only, no complexity added).",
